// @test regression/lint-repainting-security
// @description REPAINTING_SECURITY: a request.security() reading the current, still-forming HTF bar is flagged. The four exemptions must stay silent: an explicit lookahead= argument, a history offset inside the expression, a history offset on the call itself, and a request that stays on the chart's timeframe. TV is silent on every line here (probed 2026-08-15, see INV144). See INV144.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects warnings: 1
// @expects warning: line=3, message=/repaints/
//@version=6
indicator("repaint lint", overlay = true)
bad = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close)
okExplicit = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close, lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_off)
okOffset = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close[1])
okDynamicOffset = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close[barstate.isrealtime ? 1 : 0])
okCallOffset = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close)[1]
okSameTf = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, timeframe.period, close)
okEmptyTf = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "", close)
plot(bad + okExplicit + okOffset + okDynamicOffset + okCallOffset + okSameTf + okEmptyTf)
